GenerationType.IDENTITY

->follows "Let the Database Do It" approach
->database handles the incrementing of the ID automatically (like an AUTO_INCREMENT column in MySQL)
How it works: JPA doesn't know the ID until after the INSERT statement is actually executed
Best for: MySQL, SQL Server, DB2

GenerationType.SEQUENCE

->follows "External Counter" approach
->database uses a counter (sequence) to generate unique IDs
How it works: JPA asks the sequence for the "next value" before it even sends the insert command
Best for: Oracle, PostgreSQL, H2

GenerationType.TABLE

->follows "Old School" approach
->JPA uses a dedicated table in database to keep track of the last used ID
How it works: JPA reads the table, increments the value, and updates it
Best for: When you need a strategy that works exactly the same across any database

GenerationType.AUTO
JPA provider (like Hibernate) picks the best strategy based on the database we are using

